{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>By the hand of YHWH in the land of Egypt.</b> That is, for if they had been in Egypt and had refused to leave, what would have been the result? They would have died, slain by YHWH. Therefore they said that they chose that HaShem would rather have put them to death in the land of Egypt for their refusal, and they would not consent to leave, and they would die of famine — according to what is said (Lamentations 4:9): ״טוֹבִים הָיוּ חַלְלֵי חֶרֶב מֵחַלְלֵי רָעָב״." "<b>When we sat by the pot of flesh, etc.</b> From here you learn that the speakers of evil speech — these are they upon whom the yoke of Egypt's burdens was not imposed, and they are the taskmasters (shotrim), for the afflicted ones, who bore the yoke of the exile, ate the bread of poverty in Egypt. And perhaps they are those inscribed in wickedness — he is Datan and Aviram." "<b>When we sat by, etc.</b> That is, and along with the meat they would eat bread to satiety, for they had meat to use as a relish (liftef) for the bread." "<b>Or</b> it may further intend, that besides the fact that they already ate bread — that is, their meal — they would add meat to eat on top of satiety. And perhaps they were precise in saying <b>by the pot</b>, etc., and did not say ״when we ate meat״, etc., to hint that they did not eat it once it was cooked and had waited, for that would impair its taste, but rather they would sit by the pot to eat it at the very moment its cooking was finished. And they hinted at this in their words, that even though He might say to them: Slaughter of your flocks and eat meat, this would not suffice in continuity as they were accustomed always to eat bread and meat." "Further, the verse will be explained as to why it prefaced by saying ״all the congregation of the children of Israel״ — by simple logic, the entire congregation would not be on an equal footing in their complaint against YHWH and against His prophet. Therefore HaShem noted two claims, corresponding to two factions that were among Israel: one demanding meat and one demanding bread. And that is His saying <b>when we sat by the pot of flesh</b> — this is the faction of the transgressors among them. And the verse began with these words because in the corruption, the worst begins first (mitchilin mehatchat). And afterward it said ״when we ate bread to satiety״, corresponding to those demanding bread to eat, for they saw themselves in a land through which no man had passed, and they could not bring themselves in spirit to wait until their Master would give them their portion."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:43.632302067Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}